-snip">The Azores are an archipelago of nine volcanic islands in the North Atlantic, about 1,400 kilometres west of mainland Portugal.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/azov"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azov.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Azov</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Azov is a town in Rostov oblast, southern Russia, on the Don near the Sea of Azov.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aztec-empire"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aztec-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aztec Empire</span><span class="enc-type">State</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aztec Empire was the Triple Alliance of Tenochtitlan, Texcoco and Tlacopan, formed in 1428 in the Valley of Mexico and dominated by the Mexica of Tenochtitlan.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/aztec-purepecha-war-of-1479"><span class="enc-name">Aztec–Purépecha war of 1479</span><span class="enc-type">Campaign · 1479</span><span class="enc-snip">The Aztec–Purépecha war of 1479 was a military campaign by the Aztec ruler Axayacatl against the Purépecha (Tarascan) kingdom to the west.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/aztlan"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/aztlan.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Aztlan</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Aztlan is the legendary homeland from which the Mexica (Aztecs) and other Nahua peoples were said to have migrated to central Mexico.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/azuay-province"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azuay-province.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Azuay Province</span><span class="enc-type">Place</span><span class="enc-snip">Azuay is a province in the southern highlands of Ecuador, with its capital at Cuenca.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/azul-ruben-dario"><span class="enc-name">Azul (Rubén Darío)</span><span class="enc-type">Work / monument</span><span class="enc-snip">Azul is a collection of short stories and poems by the Nicaraguan poet Rubén Darío, published in Valparaíso, Chile, in 1888.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item"><a href="/encyclopedia/azzan-ibn-qais"><span class="enc-name">Azzan ibn Qais</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Azzan ibn Qais was a member of the Al Bu Said family who, backed by the Ibadi religious leaders of the Omani interior, took Muscat in 1868 and was elected imam.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/azzo-vii-deste"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azzo-vii-deste.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Azzo VII d'Este</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Azzo VII d'Este, called Novello, was marquis of Este and leader of the Guelph party in north-eastern Italy.</span></a></li><li class="enc-item has-img"><a href="/encyclopedia/azzone-visconti"><img class="enc-thumb" src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/azzone-visconti.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="56" height="56"><span class="enc-name">Azzone Visconti</span><span class="enc-type">Person</span><span class="enc-snip">Azzone Visconti was lord of Milan from 1329 to 1339.</span></a></li></ul>
